<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

	<ThingDef ParentName="CGF1_MWP_ATLauncher_T3">
		<defName>CGF1_MWP_Type51_Bazooka_</defName>
		<label>Type 51 Bazooka</label>
		<description>Caliber: 89mm M20. 1-round tube. Single-Shot.

The Type 51 is a Chinese copy of the American M20 "Super Bazooka" produced in the 1950s. The PLA captured large numbers of earlier M1, M1A1, &amp; M9 Bazooka launchers from Republic of China forces during the Chinese Civil War, but the earlier designs rapidly became obsolete in the anti-tank role due to improvements in tank protection. Accordingly, Chinese engineers acquired samples of the American M20, in the larger 89mm caliber, and reverse-engineered it to produce the Type 51. However, the Type 51 also became obsolete rather quickly, and was replaced in service by the Chinese copy of the Soviet RPG-2, known as the Type 56.</description>
